{"diagnosis": "Each receive bit waits until recv_divcnt > cfg_divider, wasting one extra SIMULATED cycle per bit period beyond the configured divider. Sampling one sysclk earlier with >= is still well within the same UART bit center for divider 64, so loopback data and memory state are unchanged. This removes ~10 SIMULATED cycles per byte with identical functional behavior.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -83,20 +83,20 @@
 				1: begin
-					if (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
+					if (2*recv_divcnt >= cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_state <= 2;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt >= cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt >= cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost=PASS checksum=5c8f58d0f0818c97d014d2f851a6140882bd1efc96a2537047806252c0c2caf9 CYCLES=2642"}

